# RawrXD runtime-generated state (audit ledger, agent session state)
.rawr/

# Certification run outputs
cert_run_output*.txt

# CMake build trees
#
# WAS: `build*/`
#
# That rule matched ANY directory whose name begins with "build", at any depth.
# It therefore excluded SOURCE directories that happen to be named "build":
#
#     rawrxd/B012/build/amortization_test.cpp
#     rawrxd/B013/build/stability_test.cpp
#     rawrxd/B014/build/b014_profiler.cpp        (+5 more)
#     rawrxd/B015/build/b015_cert_test.cpp
#
# All eight are referenced by rawrxd/CMakeLists.txt. Measured consequence: a
# clean `git worktree add` of the pushed branch FAILS to configure with
# "Cannot find source file" on exactly those paths, while a build inside the
# existing working tree succeeds because the files are present but ignored.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the fix is
# to stop excluding the directory rather than to negate files inside it. The
# rules below anchor the pattern to the repository root and to the known CMake
# tree names, which is what the original comment always intended.
/build/
/build_*/
/_build*/
/rawrxd/build/
/rawrxd/build*/
/CMakeFiles/

# Build trees that the anchored rules above no longer catch, listed explicitly.
# Each was verified to be a generated tree, not a source directory named
# "build". The B012-B015 source directories are deliberately NOT listed here:
# they are compiled by rawrxd/CMakeLists.txt and excluding them is what made a
# clean clone of beacon-residency-001 fail to configure.
/_fleet_build/
/_d2sl/
/_n2_stage/src/build/
/rawrxd/build2/
/rawrxd/src/deep2/build/
# RAWRXD_SOURCE_DURABILITY_001
# `/rawrxd/src/build/` was here and has been REMOVED.
#
# It is a SOURCE directory, not a generated tree. It holds exactly two files:
#     rawrxd/src/build/BuildIntelligence.cpp   15,421 bytes
#     rawrxd/src/build/BuildIntelligence.hpp    5,175 bytes
# rawrxd/src/build/BuildIntelligence.cpp is referenced by rawrxd/CMakeLists.txt
# and is compiled into the RawrXD_Gold target, so excluding it produced a source
# file that the build graph requires and version control could not deliver.
# Measured before this change:
#     git check-ignore rawrxd/src/build/BuildIntelligence.cpp  -> ignored (line 44)
#     git ls-files rawrxd/src/build/                            -> 0 files
# A clean checkout therefore lost a required translation unit, and `git clean
# -xdf` would delete live source with no recovery path.
#
# This is the same defect, and the same remedy, as the B012-B015 source
# directories documented at line 37 above: the rule was a build-output pattern
# that happened to match a source directory sharing its name. Per the note at
# line 24, Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so
# the fix is to stop excluding the directory -- not to negate files inside it.
#
# The genuinely generated neighbours are still excluded, deliberately:
#   /rawrxd/src/deep2/build/            holds only a .receipt.txt and a .sha256
#   /rawrxd/win32ide_strict/build*/     a CMake build tree (CMakeCache.txt,
#                                       ALL_BUILD.vcxproj, cmake_install.cmake)
#   rawrxd/src/masm/build/              only .exe and .obj output
#   rawrxd/src/remote64/build/          only .obj output
# Those four were each verified to contain no source that the build graph needs.
/rawrxd/win32ide_strict/build*/
/rawrxd_screenpilot_agent_bridge/*/build/
!build_p2/Release/rawr_monolith.exe
rawrxd/src/deep2/vulkan_compute_tmp.cpp

