# --- Repository hygiene: oracle dumps, configure trees, scratch, weights ---
#
# Everything below is regenerable by re-running the harness that produced it,
# or is local-only build state. None of it is source, and none of it is
# evidence that cannot be reproduced on demand.
#
# Anchored with a leading `/` on purpose. The rules above are unanchored and
# match at any depth; these are root-only, so a source directory or test
# fixture whose name happens to contain "build", "oracle" or "cases" is never
# swept up by them. The nqb_cases/ fixtures below are the concrete case: the
# `/*.nqb` rule is anchored to the root so those tracked fixtures survive.

# Generated parity/oracle dumps from QORACLE_001 and successor sweeps.
/_qoracle/

# CMake configure trees (CMakeCache.txt, build.ninja, CMakeFiles/, .ninja_*).
# Distinguished from /build/ and /rawrxd/build*/ above by the _cfg_ prefix.
# These are build output, not source: they regenerate on every configure.
/_cfg_*/

# Root-level CMakeCache.txt, produced by an in-source `cmake .` run at the
# repository root. Configure output. Anchored to root because rawrxd/ and the
# B0xx source directories legitimately hold sources of that name elsewhere.
# NOTE: a copy is already TRACKED, so this rule does not untrack it; see the
# audit_tombstone_001 note above for why an ignore rule cannot govern a
# tracked path. Untracking it is a separate `git rm --cached` decision.
/CMakeCache.txt
/CMakeFiles/
/cmake_install.cmake
/DartConfiguration.tcl
/Testing/

# Tombstone/staging scratch for the stub census. Superseded by
# rawrxd/audit/RAWRXD_SOURCE_INTEGRITY_AUTHORITY_001/, which is tracked.
#
# NOTE: 66 files under this directory are ALREADY TRACKED and remain so. An
# ignore rule cannot govern a tracked path, so this entry does NOT untrack or
# unstage them; it only stops NEW scratch files here from being added. The
# tracked set includes a 1.64 MiB fbst_nqb.txt / fbst_gguf.txt duplicated
# across nqb_cmp/, nqb_life/, nqb_kv/ and nqb_fbst/ (~12.7 MiB of regenerable
# dumps). They are already in history, so untracking them would not shrink it;
# if that evidence should stop being updated, it needs an explicit
# `git rm --cached` decision rather than an ignore rule.
/audit_tombstone_001/

# Root-level scratch from interactive gate sessions: logs, captured stdout,
# token/logit dumps, symbol tables, helper scripts and ad-hoc cmake snippets.
# Only the root is matched, so nothing under src/, rawrxd/ or audit/ is
# affected by these.
_*.txt
_*.log
_*.csv
_*.tokens
_*.logits
_*.sha256
_*.ps1
_*.cmake

# Locally converted NQB model weights and vocab sidecars at the repository
# root. These are multi-hundred-MiB to multi-GiB build products of the
# converter, not distributable source; the reproducible path is the converter
# plus its inputs, which ARE tracked. Anchored to root so nqb_cases/*.nqb
# regression fixtures remain tracked.
/*.nqb
/*.nqb.vocab.txt
/_*.nqb
